      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "MrDarkRoot",
        "email": "effortsmiyuki@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-10-08T05:25:44Z"
      },
      "message": "docs(review): record #209 recovery-semantics evidence\n\nRound-3 verification of PR #220 (issue #209). No production change: the\ntransient unreadable_product_data retry was traced end to end and shown to\nre-run the full fenced precondition sequence before any save, with the\ndurable journal PENDING state as the only retry gate.\n\n- docs/review/209/IMPLEMENTATION.md: recovery-semantics matrix\n  (reason -> durable journal/item state -> retryable? -> guard), the seven\n  required proofs with branch-HEAD citations, re-verification receipts, and\n  the explicit founder-approval note for the transient retry divergence.\n- tests/durable/cache-public-integration.php: transient refusal leaves\n  durable PENDING with zero saves; retry applies once; a concurrent edit\n  between attempts wins as CONFLICT with zero overwrite.\n- tests/jobs/integration.php: killed worker between checkpoints recovers to\n  APPLIED with one net price change; transient refusal at the job boundary\n  returns to PENDING with backoff and the retry re-runs the precondition.\n- tests/jobs/worker.php: test-only public woocommerce_product_class fault\n  knob used by those durable fixtures.",
      "tree": {
